----------------------------------------------------
  Moca 0.3
-----------------------------------------------------

Moca is a first-order theorem prover.

-----------------------------------------------------
  PREREQUISITE
-----------------------------------------------------

We assume that the followings have been installed.

  Z3 >= 4.6.0: https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3
  ghc >= 8.0.2
  stack >= 1.6.5

------------------------------------------------------
  HOW TO COMPILE
------------------------------------------------------

The executable file "moca" can be produced by executing

  $ stack install

in this directory.

------------------------------------------------------
  HOW TO RUN
------------------------------------------------------

  $ ./moca.sh <file> <options>

For instance,

  $ ./moca.sh problem.trs

See also the help message:

  $ ./moca.sh --help

Note:
  The shell file "moca.sh" creates tempfiles, execute moca with 59s timeout, and remove the tempfiles.
  If you directly execute "moca", tempfiles may remain undeleted.

------------------------------------------------------
  OPTIONS
------------------------------------------------------

  --siav  use the split-if encoding using all variables in s = t => u = v
  --smsi  skip execution for parameters with the multi-split-if encoding mode
  -nap    execute without approximations by projection
  -nag    execute without approximations by generalization
  --cert  generate a certificate for CPF3 (cannot be combined with other options)
  --help  Display list of options

Examples
- execute using the Claessen-Smallbone's split-if encoding:
  $ ./moca.sh problem.trs --siav --smsi 
- execute using an improved split-if encoding but not using the multi-split-if encoding:
  $ ./moca.sh problem.trs --smsi
- execute using no approximation:
  $ ./moca.sh problem.trs -nap -nag 
- execute using only the approximation by generalization:
  $ ./moca.sh problem.trs -nap 
- execute using only the approximation by projection:
  $ ./moca.sh problem.trs -nag 
- generate a certificate in CPF3:
  $ ./moca.sh --cert problem.trs > proof.xml
  $ ceta proof.xml 
